    "body": "I think that's the most reasonable interpretation; i.e. saying that \"the 'auto' value must not be used\" means that if it *is* used it will simply be regarded as invalid, just like any other unrecognized value. Perhaps this could be stated more explicitly, along the lines of \"Note that the 'auto' value is not valid for the dir attribute on this element\".\r\n\r\n(I have a patch for Gecko awaiting review in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1471872 to fix this, and have filed https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=857409 to raise the issue in Blink.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
