    "updated_at": "2018-06-30T08:13:57Z",
    "body": "@domenic  In response to the proposed Gecko patch, @upsuper  suggests[1] that as the authoring requirement that \"auto must not be used\" doesn't impose any rendering requirement on UAs, and nothing else requires `bdo` to be handled differently from other elements with regard to dir-attribute handling, the existing behavior is correct and doesn't need any change.\r\n\r\nWDYT? Given that this can affect, for example, the display of currency values (see [2] for the real-world example that brought it up) it's an interop problem that we need to figure out one way or another.\r\n\r\n[1] https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1471872#c3\r\n[2] https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1471180",
