      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2018-07-01T12:50:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-07-01T12:51:14Z",
    "body": "Yes, but in general dir=auto is not equivalent to dir=asdf, because of the rules in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#the-dir-attribute for determining the directionality of the element.\r\n\r\nSo my question remains, is it correct for the browser to apply those rules to a bdo element with dir=auto (as Firefox does), resulting in RTL directionality for the example in https://jfkthame.github.io/test/bdo.html and overriding the normal LTR-ness of the digits there?\r\n\r\nOr is it correct for the browser to ignore dir=auto on a bdo element (as MS Edge does), on the grounds that authors were explicitly told it must not be used, resulting in LTR directionality and overriding the normal RTL-ness of the Arabic letters there?\r\n\r\n(I can't think of a way to read the spec such that bidi overriding doesn't apply to the bdo element at all, though that seems to be what Webkit and Blink currently do.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/401604796/reactions",
