    "created_at": "2018-07-02T17:59:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-07-02T17:59:04Z",
    "body": "`bdo` with `dir=auto` is semantically unintelligible. It's probably reasonable to think that the user intended to use `bdi` or to apply `unicode-bidi` because that is a reasonably common mistake. But the normal effect of `bdo` is so potentially damaging to the text that ignoring the override might actually be the best thing (even if forcing LTR might help people understand that they are doing it wrong... ;-))",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
